Macedonia held a referendum to change the country's name.
A vote on whether to change the country's name to "Republic of North Macedonia" will take place on Sunday.
The referendum was organized to resolve a decades-long dispute with neighbouring Greece, which has a region called Macedonia in the country.
For many years, Greece has argued that the names of its northern neighbors are worthy of its claims of ownership over Greek territory, and it has firmly opposed Macedonia's accession to the EU and NATO.
Macedonian President Jorge Ivanov, who is opposed to a country-name-change referendum, said he intends to ignore the outcome of the vote.
But supporters of the referendum, including Prime Minister Zoran Zayev, argue that the name change would be the cost of joining the EU and Nato.
