"He said he wanted to prove to himself that it was of some value." He wanted to make sure he didn't disappoint everyone, even if the sexuality was revealed one day.
Daley, a two-time bronze medalist at the Olympics, has become an influential LGBT campaign participant, who appeared at the Commonwealth Games held in Australia this year and appealed to more countries to legitimize homosexuality.
Daley said he was lucky to be able to live without hindrance while keeping his sexuality open, and that he decided to take the plunge to give “hope” to others.
